{"ranking": ["M4", "M3", "M2"], "fault": "M4 (cascode output device) width is oversized: W=389.2 um gives M4/M3 = 26x instead of the 4x ratio needed to match the reference cascode (~59.8 um). M4 then runs at very low current density, Vgs=0.738 with Vov about 0.018 V, and Vds=0.146 V close to Vdsat=0.071 V. Its gm/gds drops to 46.6 versus about 170 for the other devices. Cascode rout ~ (gm/gds)_M4 x ro_M2 ~ 46.6 x 140 kOhm ~ 6.5 MOhm, which matches the 6.1 MOhm measured and explains the rout failure. Iout error and compliance still pass because the mirror ratio and headroom are not badly affected. Fix: set M4 W to about 60 um."}
